[?2004l[?2004h> # Performance Fix Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Problem
[?2004l[?2004h> - Validator was running at ~40 docs/sec instead of target 400-500 docs/sec
[?2004l[?2004h> - Previous caching attempt didn't help because the cache wasn't being used
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Root Causes
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **validate_document() was calling preprocess_schema() directly** - This spawned a new jq subprocess for EVERY validation
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **No validator caching** - Draft7Validator was recompiled for every document, even when using the same schema
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **get_cached_schema() existed but was never called** - The caching infrastructure was there but unused
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Solution
[?2004l[?2004h> Added get_validator() function that:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Caches compiled Draft7Validator objects per schema path
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Uses get_cached_schema() to avoid repeated jq calls
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Returns cached validators on subsequent calls
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Changed validate_document() to use get_validator() instead of directly calling preprocess_schema()
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Results
[?2004l[?2004h> - Before: 40.3 docs/sec
[?2004l[?2004h> - After (first run): 1,389.4 docs/sec (34x improvement)
[?2004l[?2004h> - After (warm cache): 10,698.7 docs/sec (265x improvement)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Target achieved**: Well above 400-500 docs/sec requirement
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Key Changes
[?2004l[?2004h> - Added _validator_cache dictionary at module level
[?2004l[?2004h> - Added get_validator() function for validator caching
[?2004l[?2004h> - Modified validate_document() to call get_validator() instead of preprocess_schema()
